WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.575
This is Flagged, and it is running entirely in your browser.

2
00:00:04.945 --> 00:00:09.769
The dashboard opens on what needs attention today, not on a list of documents.

3
00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:15.618
Three documents are not valid. Twelve need action. And eight rows are not on file at all.

4
00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:21.268
Not valid is a question, so it is a link. It opens the ships it is talking about.

5
00:00:21.638 --> 00:00:27.383
Inside a ship, every certificate carries the rule behind it and the next thing that has to happen.

6
00:00:27.753 --> 00:00:34.612
A date on its own says very little. This one expired ten days ago, and the renewal is already with the consulate.

7
00:00:34.982 --> 00:00:39.328
The steps are the record. Tick one off, and the progress follows.

8
00:00:39.698 --> 00:00:44.462
The calendar puts every expiry and every survey window on a single timeline.

9
00:00:44.832 --> 00:00:51.514
Then back to the one question the product exists to answer: what needs attention, before it becomes a problem.
